A Keeper provider call is capped past its own per-call total-duration ceiling, beside the idle-progress
watchdog of 0003 (contract §135.29's SL-69 addendum). Amended by SL-82 (§135.29 addendum 2):
`keeperCallCapMs` also accepts a zero-argument function, resolved fresh immediately before every attempt,
so a per-turn host can size one call's cap differently from the rest without the vendored session ever
being taught what a turn is.
Base: 0003 applied. Apply with: git apply -p1 from the repository root.

